=== min_heap_ops L0 #0 type=list k=None
A heap is a row of numbers in positions 1, 2, 3, ... where the number in position p is never larger than the numbers in positions 2p and 2p+1 (when those exist). To add a number: put it in the first free position at the end, then, while it is smaller than the number in position (its position divided by 2, rounded down), swap the two. To remove the smallest: take out the number in position 1, put the number from the last position into position 1 (the row is now one shorter), then, while it is larger than the smaller of the numbers in positions 2p and 2p+1 (those that exist), swap it with that smaller number. Start with an empty heap and add these numbers in order: 70, 93, 83, 81, 1, 95, 18, 63, 35, 59. Then remove the smallest 1 time. Give the row from position 1 to the end, separated by commas.
--> ANSWER: '18, 35, 81, 63, 59, 95, 83, 93, 70'
